r":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Three layers (Irish UCITS ETF/ETF share class, as of 6 Nov 2026):**\n\n1. **Transparency-policy disclosure:** The prospectus and website must state what holdings are published, how often, with what lag, and where. This applies under either route.\n\n2. **Daily public holdings (default):** Full holdings are published daily on a freely accessible website. This was the historical CBI expectation, including for active ETFs.\n\n3. **Conditional periodic route (CBI Q&A 1012, April 2025):** Holdings may instead be published periodically (e.g., quarterly, with a lag), but only if the ETF:\n   - gives authorised participants and market makers daily portfolio information for effective arbitrage,\n   - keeps the secondary-market price close to iNAV/NAV, and\n   - discloses this arrangement and its risks in the prospectus.\n\n**Caveat:** I cannot verify the 2026 regulations cited in your bank draft. Check their provisions and numbering against the published Statutory Instrument and current CBI Q&A text.","ttft_ms":3739,"type":"result","duration_ms":3755,"uuid":"f04b08ce-eaef-460c-b285-206b8df458d4","ttft_stream_ms":1293,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1293,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
